messages.content:
Analyze the Jira bug report title and description and the seed changes that were made to fix the reported bug. Combine this analysis with the initial static impact set, which contains the fully qualified names of code entities that are statically related to the seed changes.
For each entity in the initial static impact set, analyze its relationship to the seed changes and collect evidence indicating whether the entity must be modified as a consequence of the seed changes.  Furthermore, identify any additional code entities that must be modified or created and collect supporting evidence.
Focus on production code, not test code or other files.
Inputs: - Jira bug report title: Disable JMX for Statement Pool - Jira bug report description: I'm using the PoolableConnectionFactory and don't care about JMX, so I don't set the dataSourceJmxName, but I want to use a pool for my PreparedStatements. The makeObject() method initializes this pool automatically (lines 224-243) but seems to forget to disable JMX completely if I don't want it, i.e. GenericKeyedObjectPoolConfig.setJmxEnabled(...) is never called and always has the default value (=true). Therefore the JMX registration happens, which can cause a problem for me because of security constraints.

Because of the way the makeObject() method is written, I have no influence on this part, so my quick solution was to disable the poolStatement option for the PoolableConnectionFactory and provide a custom ConnectionFactory object instead that basically does the same thing with the statement pool and also disables the JMX option. - Seed changes and their Git diff hunks: [{"fqn": "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.managed.PoolableManagedConnectionFactory.makeObject()", "git_diff_hunk": "@@ -70 +71 @@ public class PoolableManagedConnectionFactory extends PoolableConnectionFactory
- if(getPoolStatements()) {
+ if (getPoolStatements()) {
@@ -77,0 +79,11 @@ public class PoolableManagedConnectionFactory extends PoolableConnectionFactory
+ ObjectName dataSourceJmxName = getDataSourceJmxName();
+ long connIndex = getConnectionIndex().getAndIncrement();
+ if (dataSourceJmxName != null) {
+ StringBuilder base = new StringBuilder(dataSourceJmxName.toString());
+ base.append(Constants.JMX_CONNECTION_BASE_EXT);
+ base.append(Long.toString(connIndex));
+ config.setJmxNameBase(base.toString());
+ config.setJmxNamePrefix(Constants.JMX_STATEMENT_POOL_PREFIX);
+ } else {
+ config.setJmxEnabled(false);
+ }"}] - Initial static code change impact set: ["org.apache.commons.dbcp2.ConnectionFactory.createConnection()", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.DelegatingConnection.setCacheState(boolean)", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.PoolableConnectionFactory(org.apache.commons.dbcp2.ConnectionFactory,javax.management.ObjectName)", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory._cacheState", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory._connFactory", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory._connectionInitSqls", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory._pool", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.getCacheState()", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.getConnectionFactory()", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.getMaxOpenPreparedStatements()", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.getPool()", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.getPoolStatements()", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.initializeConnection(java.sql.Connection)", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.maxOpenPreparedStatements", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.poolStatements", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.setCacheState(boolean)", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.setConnectionInitSql(java.util.Collection)", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.setMaxOpenPrepatedStatements(int)", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.setPool(org.apache.commons.pool2.ObjectPool)", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolableConnectionFactory.setPoolStatements(boolean)", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolingConnection.PoolingConnection(java.sql.Connection)", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.PoolingConnection.setStatementPool(org.apache.commons.pool2.KeyedObjectPool)", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.managed.PoolableManagedConnectionFactory.PoolableManagedConnectionFactory(org.apache.commons.dbcp2.managed.XAConnectionFactory,javax.management.ObjectName)", "org.apache.commons.dbcp2.managed.PoolableManagedConnectionFactory.transactionRegistry"]

Expected output:
Structured evidence for each entity of the initial static impact set, including: - its fully qualified name - an assessment of whether it must be modified as a consequence of the seed changes - the supporting evidence
Additionally, include any code entities that must be modified or created but are not part of the initial static impact set.
